{"question_text": {"Anatomy": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Which is not a rotator cuff muscle? ", "option1": "Supraspinatus ", "option2": "Teres minor ", "option3": "Infraspinatus ", "option4": "Subclavius ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Rotator_cuff_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"610\" />"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Which is the site of maturation of spermatozoa? ", "option1": "Vas deferens ", "option2": "Seminal vesicles ", "option3": "Testes ", "option4": "Epididymis ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<strong>- Epididymis acts as reservoir of spermatozoa.</strong><br /><strong>- During the storage period, the spermatozoa become mature &amp;&nbsp; motile.<br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/criteria_of_human_spermatozoa.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"805\" height=\"518\" /><br /></strong>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Continuous capillaries are found in-", "option1": "Connective tissue ", "option2": "Endocrine glands ", "option3": "Intestinal villi ", "option4": "Anterior pituitary ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Capillaries_LMCQ_CyJa0kx.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1662\" height=\"916\" />"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Gap junctions are present in-", "option1": "Skeletal muscle", "option2": "Urinary bladder ", "option3": "Smooth muscle ", "option4": "Alveoli ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<strong>*** Skeletal muscle has no cell junction.</strong><br /><strong>*** Alveoli have tight junctions.&nbsp;</strong><br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Intracellular_adhesions_table_hYzheby.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"642\" />"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Which vein is preferred for hemodialysis? ", "option1": "Axillary vein ", "option2": "Cephalic vein ", "option3": "Basilic vein ", "option4": "Median cubital vein ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Veins_of_upper_limb.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"562\" />"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Germinal epithelium lining the ovarian cortex is an example of- ", "option1": "Simple cuboidal epithelium ", "option2": "Simple squamous epithelium ", "option3": "Stratified cuboidal epithelium ", "option4": "Simple columnar epithelium ", "answer": "1", "exp": "Ovarian cortex is covered by the germinal epithelium which is made up of a <strong>single layer of cuboidal cells in younger age.</strong>&nbsp;<br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Simple_squamous__cuboidal_epithelium_.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1630\" height=\"938\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/simple_columnar_epithelium_VrGIoWG.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1600\" height=\"541\" />"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Melanocytes develop from-", "option1": "Epidermis ", "option2": "Lateral plate mesoderm ", "option3": "Neural crest ", "option4": "Dermis ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Neural_crest_LMCQ_FuZczz2.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1641\" height=\"943\" />"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) The superolateral surface of the cerebrum is supplied mainly by the-", "option1": "Anterior cerebral artery ", "option2": "Middle cerebral artery ", "option3": "Posterior cerebral artery ", "option4": "Basilar artery ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Brain_superolateral_surface_BS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1655\" height=\"732\" />"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) Skeletal muscle has-", "option1": "Fusiform cells", "option2": "Intercalated disc", "option3": "Branching fibres", "option4": "Limited regeneration capacity", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/muscle_tissue_x6epz14.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"629\" />"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Which nerve is commonly injured in humeral neck fractures? ", "option1": "Radial nerve ", "option2": "Median nerve ", "option3": "Axillary nerve ", "option4": "Musculocutaneous nerve ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<u><strong>Nerves directly related to humerus</strong></u><br /><em><strong>Three nerves are closely related to the humerus and susceptible to injury following fracture/dislocation of the corresponding parts</strong></em><br />a.<strong> Axillary nerve </strong>around the surgical neck<br />b. <strong>Radial nerve </strong>in the radial/spiral groove<br />c. <strong>Ulnar nerve</strong> behind the medial epicondyle"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Which is not a content of the broad ligament of the uterus? ", "option1": "Ovary ", "option2": "Fallopian tube ", "option3": "Ovarian artery ", "option4": "Gartner's duct ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Broad_ligament_contents_.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1151\" height=\"1163\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Which is not a barrier of the oocyte? ", "option1": "Corona radiata", "option2": "Syncytiotrophoblast ", "option3": "Zona pellucida ", "option4": "Vitelline membrane ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<u><strong>The barriers of an oocyte are</strong></u><br />1. First barrier is formed by cells of <strong>corona radiata</strong><br />2. Second barrier is formed by<strong> zona pellucida </strong>made of glycoproteins, ZP1, ZP2, and ZP3.<br />3. Third barrier is formed by <strong>vitelline membrane</strong> of oocyte itself"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) The internal capsule of the brain is an example of-", "option1": "Association fibres ", "option2": "Projection fibres ", "option3": "Commissural fibres ", "option4": "Grey matter ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/White_matters_of_cerebrum_8WSCuHV.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"936\" />"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) 'M' cells are found in-", "option1": "Thymus ", "option2": "Intestine ", "option3": "Spleen ", "option4": "Lymph nodes", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/lymphoid_organs_difference_kGveNL0.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"706\" />"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) The carotid sheath is pierced by-", "option1": "External carotid artery ", "option2": "Internal carotid artery ", "option3": "External jugular vein ", "option4": "Internal jugular vein  ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/carotid_sheath_mhs.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"564\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Carotid_sheath_mhs_2.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"527\" />"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Which nerve is closely related to the superior thyroid artery? ", "option1": "Superior laryngeal nerve ", "option2": "Recurrent laryngeal nerve ", "option3": "External laryngeal nerve ", "option4": "Internal laryngeal nerve ", "answer": "3", "exp": "The <strong>recurrent laryngeal nerve</strong> is closely related to the <strong>inferior thyroid artery</strong> and any damage to it during surgery may result in hoarse ness of the voice.&nbsp;<br /><br />Injury to the <strong>external laryngeal nerve</strong> is more common because of its <em><strong>proximity to the superior thyroid artery</strong></em>. This leads to <em><strong>loss of tension in the vocal cord with diminished power and range in the voice.</strong></em> Patients, particularly those who use their voice professionally, must be advised that any thyroid operation will result in change to the voice even in the absence of nerve trauma.&nbsp;<br /><br /><strong>[Ref. Bailey &amp; Love's 27th, Page 865]&nbsp;</strong>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) Which is the normal site of implantation of the blastocyst? ", "option1": "Ampullary region of fallopian tube ", "option2": "Anterior wall of the uterus", "option3": "Isthmus of uterus ", "option4": "Posterior wall of the uterus near fundus", "answer": "4", "exp": "The adherence and attachment of blastocyst to the endometrium is referred to as implantation.<br /><strong>&bull; Site:</strong> Normal site is <em><strong>posterior wall of the uterus close to the fundus</strong></em><br /><strong>&bull; Time: </strong>The process begins 6 7 days after ovulation and completed by 11 12 th day when the blastocyst is completely embedded in the stroma of the compact layer of endometrium."}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Lesion in the basal ganglia is not associated with-", "option1": "Parkinson's disease ", "option2": "Huntington's disease ", "option3": "Chorea ", "option4": "Difficulty in speech ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Basal_ganglia_lesions.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"580\" />"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) Which is a primary lymphoid organ? ", "option1": "Lymph node ", "option2": "Bone marrow ", "option3": "Spleen ", "option4": "Peyer's patches ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Primary__Secondary_lymphoid_organ.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"538\" />"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Anterior compartment of the foramen magnum transmits-", "option1": "Medulla oblongata", "option2": "Anterior spinal artery ", "option3": "Apical ligament of dens ", "option4": "Spinal accessory nerve ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/foramen_magnum.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"933\" />"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Which is the main source of arterial supply to the breast? ", "option1": "Posterior intercostal arteries ", "option2": "Internal thoracic artery ", "option3": "Lateral thoracic artery ", "option4": "Acromiothoracic artery ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Breast_blood_supply_LMCq.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1675\" height=\"647\" />"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) The uterine cervix develops from the-", "option1": "Cloaca ", "option2": "Mullerian duct ", "option3": "Wollfian duct ", "option4": "Urachus ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Paramesonephric_duct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"167\" />"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) The limbic system is concerned with-", "option1": "Neurosecretion ", "option2": "Temperature regulation ", "option3": "Sexual bheaviour ", "option4": "Visual processing ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Limbic_system_functions_MHS_SPeCNo0.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"477\" />"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) Which is an example of ellipsoid joint? ", "option1": "Atlanto-occipital joint ", "option2": "Ankle joint ", "option3": "Distal radioulnar joint ", "option4": "Atlanto-axial joint ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Synovial_joint_examples_zPPD628.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1665\" height=\"1637\" />"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) The transpyloric plane passes through the-", "option1": "Tip of 10th costal cartilage ", "option2": "Upper border of L1 vertebra ", "option3": "Lower part of hilus of right kidney ", "option4": "Fundus of the gall bladder ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Transpyloric_plane.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1236\" height=\"600\" />"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Which is not a content of the axilla? ", "option1": "Axillary vein ", "option2": "Roots of brachial plexus ", "option3": "Intercostobrachial nerve ", "option4": "Long thoracic nerve ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/axilla_contents_HOE50zd.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1636\" height=\"1077\" />"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Which is not a midgut derivative? ", "option1": "Lower half of duodenum ", "option2": "Pancreas ", "option3": "Hepatic flexure of colon ", "option4": "Ileum ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/primitive_gut_derivatives_FrYzaDO.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"583\" />"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) Nephrons of the kidney develops from-", "option1": "Mesonephric duct ", "option2": "Paramesonephric duct ", "option3": "Metanephros ", "option4": "Pronephros ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<u><strong>Metanephros Gives rise to nephrons</strong></u> i.e. secretory/excretory part of the kidneys<br />&bull; Bowman&rsquo;s capsule<br />&bull; Glomerulus<br />&bull; PCT<br />&bull; Loop of Henle<br />&bull; DCT<br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Mesonephric_duct_F1bwyLv.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"370\" />"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Which is the main inorganic component of the bones? ", "option1": "Type-I collagen fibres ", "option2": "Calcium carbonate ", "option3": "Calcium phosphate ", "option4": "Calcium fluoride", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Bone_composition.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1645\" height=\"950\" />"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) What is the root value of the cremasteric reflex? ", "option1": "L1, L2 ", "option2": "S1, S2 ", "option3": "L3, L4 ", "option4": "L5, S1", "answer": "1", "exp": "<u><strong>Cremasteric muscle:</strong></u>&nbsp;<br />Well developed in male, <em><strong>Derived from internal oblique &amp; transversus abdominis</strong></em><br /> <strong>Nerve supply:</strong> <em><strong>Genital branch of genitofemoral nerve (L1, L2)</strong></em><br /> Action: Pull the testes, Cremester reflex, thermo regulation of testes<br /><strong> Cremasteric reflex:</strong> Root value <em><strong>L1, L2</strong></em><br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/common_jerks.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"522\" />"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) Which is not true regarding the sternal angle? ", "option1": "Pulmonary trunk bifurcates just below this level ", "option2": "Arch of aorta ends at this level ", "option3": "Trachea bifurcates at this level ", "option4": "Ascending aorta begins at this level ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/sternal_angle.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1870\" height=\"1610\" />"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Medial medullary syndrome results in-", "option1": "Ipsilateral spastic paralysis ", "option2": "Contralateral loss of pain & temperature", "option3": "Horner's syndrome ", "option4": "Contralateral spastic paralysis ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Medial_medullary_syndrome_MHS.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"516\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Lateral_medullary_syndrome_MHS_eo6zTjK.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"404\" />"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) Which gland is mesodermal in origin? ", "option1": "Posterior pituitary ", "option2": "Adrenal medulla ", "option3": "Liver ", "option4": "Adrenal cortex ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Major_glands_origin_jKARzJG.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"383\" />"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) Type-IV collagen fibres are found in- ", "option1": "Cartilage ", "option2": "Vitreous body ", "option3": "Placenta ", "option4": "Basal lamina ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/collagen_fibres.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1088\" />"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) The deep inguinal ring is a defect in the-", "option1": "Transversus abdominis aponeurosis", "option2": "Internal oblique aponeurosis ", "option3": "Fascia transversalis ", "option4": "External oblique aponeurosis ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Inguinal_rings_LMCQ.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"841\" />"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) Which is a content of both posterior and middle mediastinum? ", "option1": "Thoracic duct ", "option2": "Esophagus ", "option3": "Azygos vein ", "option4": "Vagus nerve ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mediastinum_contents_rLEpBOC.PNG\" alt=\"\" width=\"851\" height=\"453\" />"}, {"id": "37", "question": "৩৭) Which is a branch of the basilar artery? ", "option1": "Posterior inferior cerebellar artery ", "option2": "Posterior communicating artery ", "option3": "Posterior cerebral artery ", "option4": "Middle cerebral artery ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Blood_supply_of_brain_MHS_VtKhqRv.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"508\" />"}, {"id": "38", "question": "৩৮) Transport of which substance through the placental membrane requires energy? ", "option1": "Amino acids", "option2": "Glucose ", "option3": "Vitamins ", "option4": "Carbon di-oxide ", "answer": "1", "exp": "Exchange of gases such as oxygen, carbon dioxide, and carbon monoxide is accomplished by <strong>simple diffusion<br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Placental_exchange_MHS_P5HPmyh.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"587\" /><br /></strong>"}, {"id": "39", "question": "৩৯) Which gland shows eccrine secretion? ", "option1": "Pancreatic acini ", "option2": "Thyroid ", "option3": "Mammary gland ", "option4": "Sebaceous gland", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/glands_based_on_mode_of_secretion_pyGi9vl.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1500\" height=\"577\" />"}, {"id": "40", "question": "৪০) The femoral sheath is formed by-", "option1": "Psoas fascia ", "option2": "Fascia iliaca ", "option3": "Fascia lata ", "option4": "Obturator fascia ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Femoral_sheath_mhs_VMDh6xY.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"734\" />"}, {"id": "41", "question": "৪১) Which of these is composed of hyaline cartilage? ", "option1": "Epiglottis ", "option2": "Arytenoid cartilage ", "option3": "Cuneiform cartilage ", "option4": "Corniculate cartilage ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Laryngeal_cartilage_.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1661\" height=\"1088\" />"}, {"id": "42", "question": "৪২) Which is a content of the cavernous sinus? ", "option1": "Abducent nerve ", "option2": "Trochlear nerve ", "option3": "Ophthalmic nerve ", "option4": "Maxillary nerve ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Cavernous_sinus_MHS2_GcDX7Jj.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"508\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/cavernous_sinus_LaPr5KB.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"449\" />"}, {"id": "43", "question": "৪৩) Immunological competence of the fetus starts to develop at-", "option1": "3 weeks ", "option2": "3 months ", "option3": "6 months ", "option4": "6 weeks ", "answer": "2", "exp": "&bull; I<strong>mmunological competence of the fetus begins to develop at around 3 months. By this time the fetus makes all the components of the complement</strong><br />&bull; Maternal IgG begins to be transported from the mother to the fetus at approx 14 weeks (3.5 months)<br />&bull; Newborns begin to produce their own antibody, but adult levels are not reached until the age of 3 years"}, {"id": "44", "question": "৪৪) Cilia has a core of- ", "option1": "Microtubules ", "option2": "Microfilaments", "option3": "Intermediate filaments ", "option4": "Actin filaments ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/specializations_of_epithelial_cell_surface.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"540\" />"}, {"id": "45", "question": "৪৫) Which is the most dependent part of the abdominal cavity above the pelvic brim in supine position? ", "option1": "Rectovesical pouch ", "option2": "Rectouterine pouch ", "option3": "Hepatorenal pouch ", "option4": "Paracolic gutter ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Hepatorenal_pouch.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"808\" />"}, {"id": "46", "question": "৪৬) The diaphragm is pierced by-", "option1": "Right phrenic nerve ", "option2": "Greater splanchnic nerve ", "option3": "Accessory hemiazygos vein ", "option4": "Thoracic duct ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<u><strong>Structures piercing the diaphragm:&nbsp;</strong></u><br />1. <em><strong>Greater, lesser, and least splanchnic nerves</strong></em> pass by piercing the crus of diaphragm on the corresponding side<br />2. <em><strong>Hemiazygos vein</strong></em> pierces the left crus of the diaphragm<br />3. <em><strong>Left phrenic nerve</strong></em> pierces left cupola"}, {"id": "47", "question": "৪৭) Blood brain barrier is present in-", "option1": "Pineal gland ", "option2": "Anterior pituitary ", "option3": "Tuber cinerum ", "option4": "Foramen of Monro ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Blood_brain_barrier_absent_in.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"728\" />"}, {"id": "48", "question": "৪৮) The medial umbilical ligament is a remnant of-", "option1": "Umbilical vein ", "option2": "Ductus arteriosus ", "option3": "Umbilical artery ", "option4": "Ductus venosus ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/remnants_cA9UC3t.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"344\" />"}, {"id": "49", "question": "৪৯) Which is not an avascular structure? ", "option1": "Epithelium  ", "option2": "Cornea ", "option3": "Cartilage ", "option4": "Nail-bed", "answer": "4", "exp": "Although the nail is an 