ratory_tract.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1195\" height=\"1133\" /><br /><br />[Ref. Junquira}"}, {"id": "63", "question": "৬৩) The medial nasal prominences fuse to form-", "option1": "Lateral part of the upper lip ", "option2": "Alae of the nose ", "option3": "Primitive palate ", "option4": "Secondary palate ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/development_of_lips_and_palate_r2c9je0.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1688\" height=\"877\" />"}, {"id": "64", "question": "৬৪) In a female who is a carrier of hemophilia, her offsprings with a normal male will be-", "option1": "All sons will be affected ", "option2": "All daughters will be carriers ", "option3": "Half of the sons will be affected ", "option4": "One-fourth of the daughters will be carriers ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<strong>Hemophilia is an X-linked recessive trait.</strong><br /><br /><u><strong>In X-linked recessive disorders-</strong></u><br />1. Affected cases are usually males carrying the gene.<br />2. Homozygous females can be affected, but this is rare.<br />3. Heterozygous females usually do not express the full phenotypic changes because of the paired normal allele.<br />4. Only females are carriers.<br />5.<strong> If a female has the allele (female carrier) with a normal male, off springs will be</strong><br /><em><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; - 50% daughters carrier, 50% normal</strong></em><br /><em><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp; - 50% sons affected, 50% normal<br /></strong></em><strong>6. If a male has the allele (affected male) with a normal female the off springs will be</strong><em><strong><br />&nbsp; &nbsp;- All daughters carrier<br />&nbsp; &nbsp;- All sons normal (no male to male</strong></em>"}, {"id": "65", "question": "৬৫) Which is the most common site of peptic ulceration? ", "option1": "Lesser curvature of stomach ", "option2": "First part of duodenum ", "option3": "Meckel's diverticulum", "option4": "Greater curvature of stomach ", "answer": "2", "exp": "Common sites for peptic ulcers are the<strong> first part of the duodenum</strong> and the <strong>lesser curve of the stomach</strong>, but they also occur on the <strong>stoma</strong> following gastric surgery, in the <strong>oesophagus</strong> and even in a <strong>Meckel&rsquo;s diverticulum</strong>, which contains ectopic gastric epithelium. In general, the ulcer occurs at a j<strong>unction between diferent types of epithelia</strong>, in the epithelium least resistant to acid damage.<br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Peptic_ulcer_BL.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"987\" height=\"880\" />"}, {"id": "66", "question": "৬৬) The lacrimal gland is supplied by-", "option1": "Pterygopalatine ganglion ", "option2": "Otic ganglion ", "option3": "Submandibular ganglion ", "option4": "Ciliary ganglion ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/parasympathetic_ganglia_MSO7jAP.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"749\" />"}, {"id": "67", "question": "৬৭) Which is a branch of the external carotid artery? ", "option1": "Inferior thyroid artery ", "option2": "Facial artery ", "option3": "Descending pharyngeal artery ", "option4": "Ascending palatine artery ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/External_carotid_artery_mhs_sHoGt4u.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"483\" />"}, {"id": "68", "question": "৬৮) Which period of gestation is most susceptible to teratogenicity? ", "option1": "First three weeks ", "option2": "Third to eighth weeks", "option3": "Twelfth to twenty fourth weeks", "option4": "Third trimester ", "answer": "2", "exp": "Birth defect, congenital malformation, and congenital anomaly are synonymous terms used to describe structural, behavioral, function